<div class="page-section"><div class="container content-section"><div class="row gx-0 gx-sm-5 gx-lg-5"><div class="col-12">
<h1>Policies &amp; Procedures</h1>
<p>These university policies and procedures outline the rights, responsibilities, and standards that guide teaching, learning, employment, and participation in the University of Hawaiʻi at Mānoa community.</p>
</div></div></div></div>
<section class="page-section page-section--gray" aria-label="Consolidated policies draft">
<div class="container content-section"><div class="row gx-0 gx-sm-5 gx-lg-5"><div class="col-12">
<h2><a href="https://www.hawaii.edu/equity/policies/eeo-policies">Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO)</a></h2>
<p>The University of Hawaiʻi provides policies and procedures addressing nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, harassment, disability access, recruitment, and hiring.</p>
<hr>
<h2><a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/catalog/about-uh/campus-policies/#academic-integrity">Academic Integrity and Plagiarism</a></h2>
<p>University guidance explains expectations for academic honesty, including acknowledging sources and avoiding plagiarism, cheating, and unauthorized use of others’ work.</p>
<hr>
<h2><a href="https://www.hawaii.edu/policy/?action=viewPolicy&amp;policySection=ep&amp;policyChapter=1&amp;policyNumber=203">Consensual Relationships</a></h2>
<p>University policy addresses consensual relationships where differences in authority may create conflicts of interest, including supervisory, instructional, and evaluative relationships.</p>
<hr>
<h2><a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/studentsuccess/academic-grievance/responsibilities-of-faculty/">Responsibilities of Faculty</a></h2>
<p>Faculty are expected to uphold professional standards in teaching, research, and other instructional settings. University guidance describes their responsibilities to students.</p>
<hr>
<h2><a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/studentsuccess/academic-grievance/">Responsibilities of Students</a></h2>
<p>Students are expected to uphold academic standards and respect the rights of others. The university’s academic grievance resources include guidance on student responsibilities.</p>
<hr>
<h2>Academic Grievances</h2>
<p>Review the <a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/studentsuccess/academic-grievance/">Division of Student Success academic grievance procedures and grade appeal process</a> and the <a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/graduate/graduate-student-complaint/">Graduate Division student complaint procedures</a> for guidance relevant to your concern.</p>
<hr>
<h2><a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/studentsuccess/conduct-code/">Student Conduct Code</a></h2>
<p>The Student Conduct Code describes expectations for student behavior and the university’s related policies and procedures.</p>
<hr>
<h2><a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/registrar/faculty-staff/ferpa-policies/">Confidentiality of Student Records</a></h2>
<p>The Office of the Registrar provides guidance on the privacy of student education records under the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA).</p>
<hr>
<h2><a href="https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/communications/tobaccofree/">Tobacco Products Policy</a></h2>
<p>University of Hawaiʻi campuses and university-owned facilities are tobacco-free. University guidance explains the restrictions and provides resources for quitting tobacco use.</p>
<hr>
<h2>Graduate Division</h2>
<h3><a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/graduate/academic-progress/index.php">Academic Progress</a></h3>
<p>Graduate students must meet their program’s coursework, grade, and academic requirements. Students completing a thesis or dissertation should keep their committees informed through regular progress reports or chapter drafts.</p>
<hr class="my-3">
<h3><a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/graduate/conduct-code/">Conduct Code</a></h3>
<p>Graduate Division guidance addresses academic conduct, disciplinary action, and professional standards that may apply to graduate students in their fields of study.</p>
</div></div></div>
</section>
